xf.help.map=World map and claims
xf.help.map.body=The marker shows your position. Drag with the left mouse button to move the map. Scroll or use + and - to zoom. Center on you returns to your position; Full map shows the whole map.\n\nUse layer buttons to show or hide roads, fields, buildings, shops, borders and claims. A + means shown. Map features may differ from blocks in the world.\n\nFaction claims use the owner's color. Safe zones are orange; war zones are red. Wilderness has no claim fill. Click a colored claim to see its city name. If another feature is selected, hide that feature's layer and click again. Colors alone may not uniquely identify a faction.\n\nLand check is optional and starts hidden. It shows land eligibility, not ownership. Map backgrounds depend on the server's world and available map images. Start here and Help remain available when the map cannot load.
xf.help.factions=Joining and running a faction
xf.help.factions.body=Browse factions, then ask to join one or create your own. An application needs approval. If you already have an invitation, use Accept invitation in Faction actions.\n\nMembers can use the faction's shared home and check its status. Officers and leaders manage applications and more faction settings. Some actions require a particular rank. The action form shows that requirement.\n\nOpen Faction actions for member management, identity, alliances and war. The server checks every request. Full command lists remain available through the Help category.
xf.help.cities=Cities and home
xf.help.cities.body=Join or create a faction first. Get a City Center asks for a city name and gives you a named City Center item. Place that item to found the city. The command alone does not claim land.\n\nYour first city becomes the capital. Officers and leaders can set the faction home inside that capital. Members can travel to the saved home when the server's travel rules allow it.\n\nCities need space and prestige. Check your capital, balance and city actions before expanding. City upgrades and moves have their own requirements; the server explains rejected actions.
xf.help.prestige=Prestige and growth
xf.help.prestige.body=Prestige is your faction's shared resource for upkeep, city growth, war and travel points. Check prestige in Faction actions to see your balance.\n\nFaction production buildings can generate prestige. Maintain enough prestige for upkeep before expanding. Costs and production depend on the server settings.\n\nEconomy and city actions let you inspect and manage these systems. Daily rewards are separate: open Daily rewards to see the wheel, available spins and pending items. Closing it does not spend a spin.
xf.help.safety=Before you fight
xf.help.safety.body=Other factions can own land and take part in wars. Check claims on the map before choosing where to settle. Map colors identify claim types; they do not explain every combat rule.\n\nStarter protection and faction build protection depend on server settings and your current status. Do not assume you are protected. Ask staff when unsure.\n\nWar and alliance actions are available in Faction actions. Read the action and its requirements before using it. Actions that need extra confirmation still ask for it.
xf.help.menus=Using the menus
xf.help.menus.body=Use the faction-menu key to reopen this menu. Its default is K; you can change it in Minecraft Controls. Assign Open Xenofactions World Map in Controls for direct map access; it starts unbound. World map and Start here are always available from the main menu.\n\nFaction actions groups related actions. Use the category arrows or search by name. Choose an action, fill in its fields, then select Use action. The > button beside a field cycles available choices. You can also type a value.\n\nPrevious and Next beside the argument count show more fields. Edit in chat opens the command for editing. Command details shows the full description, syntax, aliases and command preview. Copy syntax copies the usage.\n\nBack returns to the previous page. Play or Escape lets you leave. Your current page is kept when you return from Help or another menu. The welcome introduction can be dismissed without reading these pages.
xf.help.replay=Only your welcome preference will change. Rewards and faction progress stay as they are.
